wer limit (0.1 W) is taken as given by inputs/requirements.txt; no part model or datasheet exists in the candidate to independently confirm the fitted part's rating.","Board connectivity evaluated against the saved zone fill; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass, so fill-state-dependent connectivity was verified as saved only.","No thermal simulation of R1 on the 0805 footprint was performed; time-to-failure or steady-state temperature under the 2.3x overload was not quantified, only the limit exceedance itself."],"findings":[{"id":"PHY-1","title":"R1 dissipates 230.4 mW continuously under the specified 48 V / clamped-output condition, 2.3x its stated 0.1 W limit","location":"R1 (10k, Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric), inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch (symbol uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78); board footprint uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5 in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb","condition":"The exercise condition in inputs/requirements.txt: external equipment holds /IN at 48 V DC and clamps /OUT to 0 V indefinitely; fitted R1 has a continuous power limit of 0.1 W.","mechanism":"R1 connects /IN (pin 1) directly to /OUT (pin 2) per the verified netlist and board pads. With /OUT clamped to 0 V off-board, the full 48 V appears across the 10 kOhm resistor: I = 4.8 mA, P = V^2/R = 48^2/10000 = 0.2304 W. This is 230% of the stated 0.1 W continuous limit, applied indefinitely, so R1 operates in sustained overload for the entire clamp duration; C1 carries no DC and provides no relief. The ngspice operating point confirms 4.8 mA and 0.2304 W dissipated in R1. The sole stated evaluation criterion is therefore failed with a 130% margin exceedance; meeting 0.1 W at 48 V would require R1 >= 23.04 kOhm.","severity":"blocking","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/requirements.txt","locator":"lines 1-2 (48 V on /IN, /OUT clamped to 0 V indefinitely, R1 continuous limit 0.1 W)"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol D